body:
@usradam Fantastic! This complements the sentiment networks of @jseto808. Presuming I see my line correctly, I can very visibly see my positivity sank to the void as the years went by if your metric is correct (I need to review). 

Jokes aside, whether we can trust the model is a problem of its own since we never got to see the accuracy of the one trained, but this is beyond the point the scope of this work. These days you can take a LLM and ask to do the task and then just plug in where pysenti predict is. The more important part I wanted your group to take from here is all the work leading to a simple story you can tell. 

Any guesses as to why we only see 3 lines? I am still working on the sentiment classifier itself. It finally decided to run thanks to @splimon passing me the transformer version and python. Them not being added to env.yml of the project last session costed me 3h+ today.
